# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## To [[search#Verb|search]] for (something) on the [[Internet]] [[use#Verb|using]] the [[Google]] [[search engine]].
##: {{ux|en|Tom '''googles''' all of his prospective girlfriends.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Larry Page|title=New Features|work=[[w:EGroups|eGroups]]|url=http://www.egroups.com/group/google-friends/3.html|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/19991009052012/www.egroups.com/group/google-friends/3.html|archivedate=9 October 1999|date=8 July 1998|passage=Have fun and keep '''googling'''!|footer={{small|This is the first occurrence of the term in print.}}}}
##* {{quote-av|en|writer=w:Kevin Wade|title=w:Maid in Manhattan|date=13 December 2002|actor=w:Jennifer Lopez|role=Marisa|passage=<!--Marisa's son cannot find the answer to a question.-->'''Google''' it.}}
##* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=w:Bill Keller|title=Who’s sorry now?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210323123828/https://www.nytimes.com/2002/12/28/opinion/who-s-sorry-now.html|archivedate=23 March 2021|date=28 December 2002|page=A-19|passage='''Googling''' in search of an apology from the former Enron C.E.O. {{w|Kenneth Lay}}, I came up with a report in the newspaper Oil Daily headlined "Lay apologizes." But tel me if you can find any remorse in his actual words: {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|by extension}} To search for (something) on the Internet using any [[comprehensive]] search engine.
##: {{ux|en|I '''googled''' him but there were no references to him on the Internet.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[locatable]] in a search of the Internet.
#: {{ux|en|His name '''googles'''.}}

